WEBVTT

00:05.330 --> 00:08.050
It's such a beautiful day.

00:08.900 --> 00:12.340
Hello, this is Fujiwara
no "Skytree" Teika.

00:12.340 --> 00:15.030
Does everyone know what
a Chokusen Wakashu is?

00:15.050 --> 00:20.140
Choku

00:15.750 --> 00:17.900
It's a poem anthology
that was compiled at

00:17.900 --> 00:19.780
the command of an emperor,
reigning or former.

00:20.140 --> 00:26.230
Shin Kokin Wakashu
Shin Chokusen Wakashu

00:20.580 --> 00:23.780
I worked on the Shin Kokin Wakashu and

00:23.780 --> 00:25.970
the Shin Chokusen Wakashu.

00:25.520 --> 00:31.340
Kokin Wakashu

00:25.970 --> 00:31.340
The first such anthology
was the Kokin Wakashu.

00:31.750 --> 00:35.130
That anthology was
compiled by this person!

00:35.730 --> 00:38.880
Ki no "Tokyo Tower" Tsurayuki-senpai!

00:38.880 --> 00:39.760
Hello.

00:39.760 --> 00:46.600
Tosa Nikki

00:40.190 --> 00:42.640
Tsurayuki-senpai wrote
more than just poems.

00:42.640 --> 00:44.290
He pretended to be a woman

00:44.290 --> 00:46.230
and wrote a diary called the Tosa Nikki.

00:46.740 --> 00:48.500
Just like some people on
the Internet nowadays.

00:48.870 --> 00:49.570
Tee-hee.

00:50.220 --> 00:54.260
Today, we have a story
from your time period!

00:54.260 --> 00:55.570
Great!

02:34.070 --> 02:35.550
So this is Mount Uji?

02:36.520 --> 02:39.490
The sight helps to relieve the fatigue
from my time in the capital,

02:40.170 --> 02:41.550
but it's so far away.

02:42.030 --> 02:45.150
Why does he live out in
the middle of nowhere?

02:45.150 --> 02:46.680
I apologize for that.

02:47.760 --> 02:50.440
It's been a while, Tsurayuki-kun.

02:50.440 --> 02:52.040
Oh, Kisen-dono.

02:52.040 --> 02:53.640
It's been a very long time.

02:53.640 --> 02:55.650
What brings you out here?

02:55.950 --> 02:59.400
I have come to seek your advice.

02:59.400 --> 03:02.910
Oh?  This old man can
still be of assistance?

03:02.910 --> 03:04.410
Of course!

03:04.410 --> 03:07.000
No matter.  Enjoy your stay.

03:07.000 --> 03:08.040
Um, yes.

03:08.760 --> 03:11.400
Anyway, this is a beautiful place.

03:11.400 --> 03:13.280
The remote location can be inconvenient,

03:13.280 --> 03:15.210
but you barely notice it after a while.

03:15.210 --> 03:17.460
The inconvenience can
be very interesting.

03:17.460 --> 03:19.060
Ki-Kisen-dono!

03:19.820 --> 03:21.910
You walk very fast...

03:21.910 --> 03:24.220
Oh, you can't keep up?

03:24.770 --> 03:27.060
You city folk are too weak.

03:29.630 --> 03:31.210
You see, the Emperor

03:31.210 --> 03:34.170
recently commissioned
a new poem anthology,

03:34.170 --> 03:36.790
so I was planning on introducing you,

03:36.790 --> 03:40.110
and five other contemporary
poets, in the preface.

03:40.400 --> 03:42.150
Ono no Komachi

03:40.400 --> 03:43.030
The Monk Henjo

03:41.590 --> 03:44.780
The Monk Henjo, Ono no Komachi,

03:42.150 --> 03:44.780
Ono no Komachi

03:42.150 --> 03:46.330
Ariwara no Narihira

03:44.780 --> 03:48.370
Ariwara no Narihira, Otomo no Kuronushi,

03:44.780 --> 03:49.950
Otomo no Kuronushi

03:46.330 --> 03:48.370
Ariwara no Narihira

03:48.370 --> 03:49.950
Funya no Yasuhide

03:48.370 --> 03:50.160
Funya no Yasuhide,

03:50.160 --> 03:53.310
and yourself, Monk Kisen.

03:53.310 --> 03:56.630
Hmm, why did you choose the six of us?

03:56.750 --> 04:02.050
Ono no Takamura

03:56.750 --> 04:02.050
Ariwara no Yukihira

03:57.260 --> 03:59.480
Why didn't you include
Narihira's elder brother,

03:59.480 --> 04:01.880
Yukihira, and Ono no Takamura?

04:02.360 --> 04:06.370
I didn't want to approach
anyone too important,

04:06.370 --> 04:08.890
since my rank is low.

04:09.470 --> 04:12.530
So you chose Yasuhide and
myself, who are also low rank.

04:12.530 --> 04:16.770
No, I was told to choose people who had

04:16.770 --> 04:18.540
ties to Prince Koretaka.

04:18.540 --> 04:19.860
What do you mean?

04:20.170 --> 04:22.650
Basically, they're scared that

04:22.650 --> 04:25.440
Prince Koretaka will curse them
for causing his downfall,

04:25.440 --> 04:27.270
so they want to appeal
to his acquaintances?

04:27.270 --> 04:28.330
Foolishness!

04:28.940 --> 04:31.740
I take no pride in being
chosen for such a reason!

04:31.740 --> 04:32.450
Find someone else!

04:32.450 --> 04:38.290
W-Wait, I chose you because I
respected your ability as poets.

04:38.660 --> 04:41.710
Unfortunately, the other
five have passed away.

04:41.710 --> 04:44.010
That is why I came to see you.

04:44.670 --> 04:48.060
Kisen-dono, could you tell me
some stories from your heyday?

04:48.060 --> 04:49.970
To help me write the preface?

04:51.820 --> 04:53.300
Very well then.

04:54.480 --> 04:57.240
This was back when the
Monk Henjo still called

04:57.240 --> 04:59.940
himself Yoshimune no Munesada-sama.

05:00.440 --> 05:03.440
Munesada and Yoshiko

05:00.440 --> 05:03.440
The Monk Henjo

05:04.180 --> 05:05.690
One hundred nights of calling?

05:05.690 --> 05:07.570
Haven't you heard, Munesada-dono?

05:07.570 --> 05:09.910
Can anyone call on Ono no Yoshizane's

05:09.910 --> 05:12.290
daughter one hundred nights in a row?

05:12.610 --> 05:14.770
There's a wager going on.

05:14.770 --> 05:17.500
Ah, a hundred nights...

05:18.360 --> 05:21.170
Has anyone wagered that
someone will succeed?

05:21.170 --> 05:23.720
Yes, she herself has.

05:23.720 --> 05:26.010
She thinks it's actually doable.

05:26.010 --> 05:27.470
How many nights did you manage?

05:27.470 --> 05:28.750
I quit after ten.

05:28.750 --> 05:29.760
I only made it five.

05:30.370 --> 05:32.040
I gave up after three.

05:32.040 --> 05:33.350
You tried?

05:33.350 --> 05:35.860
It's quite discouraging
to make the trek

05:35.860 --> 05:37.980
after a hard day's work.

05:37.980 --> 05:39.010
It's too arrogant

05:39.010 --> 05:41.850
to demand that a man call
on her one hundred nights

05:41.850 --> 05:43.320
in a row to win her hand.

05:43.320 --> 05:45.010
She's just putting on airs.

05:45.010 --> 05:47.410
She's probably nothing
more than a homely woman.

05:47.410 --> 05:48.470
That's not true.

05:49.370 --> 05:52.910
Her beauty is worth the effort.

05:56.250 --> 06:00.620
So spring ends and summer comes,

06:01.250 --> 06:04.400
now white robes hang to
dry on Mount Amanokagu.

06:05.400 --> 06:08.100
That's a poem by Empress Jito, Yoshiko.

06:08.100 --> 06:08.840
Yes,

06:09.890 --> 06:11.190
dear brother.

06:12.760 --> 06:15.550
In that case, you should give it a try.

06:15.550 --> 06:15.930
Huh?

06:15.930 --> 06:17.260
I'm guessing you've been

06:17.260 --> 06:19.270
egging men on and ridiculing
them when they fail.

06:19.270 --> 06:21.910
No, this is the first time I've
heard about the practice.

06:21.910 --> 06:23.770
You're obligated to try it now.

06:23.770 --> 06:25.030
Obligated?

06:25.530 --> 06:27.230
Besides, it's obviously
impossible to call on her

06:27.230 --> 06:28.600
one hundred nights in a row.

06:28.600 --> 06:30.230
That doesn't solve anything.

06:30.230 --> 06:31.140
Curses!

06:31.140 --> 06:34.990
I won't be happy until
I see someone succeed!

06:34.990 --> 06:37.520
However, the offer won't
last much longer.

06:37.520 --> 06:38.530
Why not?

06:38.530 --> 06:40.560
There are plenty of people
who haven't tried yet.

06:40.560 --> 06:42.890
Well, I've heard that Yoshizane-dono

06:42.890 --> 06:45.250
intends to send his
daughter to the palace.

06:46.130 --> 06:47.460
The palace?

06:47.460 --> 06:49.120
To become one of the Emperor's brides?

06:49.120 --> 06:51.970
If she pleases the Emperor
during the Gosechi Dance

06:51.970 --> 06:54.550
at the Harvest Festival...

06:55.160 --> 06:58.810
Yoshiko will be wed to the Emperor?

07:11.870 --> 07:13.210
Yoshiko-sama.

07:14.400 --> 07:17.640
You never visit this late, dear brother.

07:17.640 --> 07:20.000
I've been busy during the day.

07:20.430 --> 07:22.440
Have you been doing well, Yoshiko?

07:22.850 --> 07:24.880
Everything is unchanged.

07:25.300 --> 07:27.400
You speak with such formality,

07:27.400 --> 07:29.420
and you've left the blinds shut.

07:29.420 --> 07:31.260
We're both grown adults.

07:32.210 --> 07:34.210
It would be shameful of me

07:34.210 --> 07:37.680
to show my face to a man,
even if it's you, dear brother.

07:39.230 --> 07:40.180
I see.

07:40.770 --> 07:46.130
Speaking of which, it seems
that many men seek your hand.

07:46.790 --> 07:50.220
Some men were talking about the
hundred nights of calling.

07:50.220 --> 07:52.030
Oh, that.

07:52.400 --> 07:58.520
The men call you arrogant
for turning down every suitor.

07:58.970 --> 08:03.410
Please, I would never insult
a man by sending him away.

08:03.410 --> 08:05.100
I have no problem with
sending away suitors,

08:05.100 --> 08:09.020
but it doesn't seem right to ask them
to call on you one hundred nights.

08:09.020 --> 08:11.360
If you're going to make
impossible demands,

08:11.360 --> 08:13.120
you should just say no.

08:13.680 --> 08:15.870
That's why they think you're arrogant.

08:15.870 --> 08:19.310
Oh, you sound as foolish
as the rest of them.

08:19.810 --> 08:21.190
Am I foolish?

08:21.660 --> 08:25.270
Once a woman is married, she will
spend the rest of her life waiting.

08:25.790 --> 08:28.810
One hundred nights may go by

08:28.810 --> 08:31.030
without seeing her husband.

08:31.770 --> 08:33.640
It would only be reasonable

08:33.640 --> 08:36.670
to expect the same from her partner.

08:37.290 --> 08:40.370
Is it arrogant of a woman
to seek happiness?

08:41.790 --> 08:45.610
I see.  So you want to be happy.

08:45.610 --> 08:47.140
Yes, that's right.

08:47.570 --> 08:48.380
I understand.

08:48.800 --> 08:51.350
Then I'll start by baring my heart.

08:51.350 --> 08:51.920
Huh?

08:52.360 --> 08:54.940
You see, I'm the next person
who's supposed to try

08:54.940 --> 08:57.390
calling on you one
hundred nights in a row.

08:57.670 --> 08:58.610
What?

08:58.610 --> 09:00.100
This would be the first.

09:00.360 --> 09:01.870
No, stop it!

09:01.870 --> 09:03.640
This isn't like you.

09:03.640 --> 09:05.760
Your friends must have
goaded you into this!

09:06.340 --> 09:09.080
So you refuse to accept my love?

09:09.470 --> 09:10.320
Love?

09:10.900 --> 09:14.340
I have always cared deeply for you.

09:14.650 --> 09:17.060
We were raised as brother and sister,

09:17.060 --> 09:19.620
so I never realized that this was love.

09:20.000 --> 09:20.990
Why?

09:21.640 --> 09:23.410
Why are you saying this now?

09:23.840 --> 09:25.830
Because I heard that you
would be sent to the palace.

09:26.740 --> 09:29.620
I realized something when
I heard that you would be

09:29.620 --> 09:31.130
taken out of my reach.

09:31.960 --> 09:34.720
I love you, Yoshiko.

09:35.410 --> 09:37.360
I won't let anyone take you from me.

09:37.360 --> 09:39.860
Not even the Emperor.

09:43.820 --> 09:45.630
I really have to call on you
one hundred nights?

09:45.630 --> 09:46.460
Yes!

09:46.460 --> 09:48.740
What?  That'll be a pain.

09:48.740 --> 09:50.070
Excuse me?!

09:50.070 --> 09:53.490
I would never leave you alone
for one hundred nights.

09:53.490 --> 09:55.110
Talk is cheap.

09:55.550 --> 10:00.330
Fine, then.
I have to prove myself first,

10:00.930 --> 10:02.910
but you should remember something.

10:04.270 --> 10:06.040
I hate to lose.

10:06.640 --> 10:08.910
I vow to call on you for
one hundred nights.

10:08.910 --> 10:11.760
So be prepared.

10:20.260 --> 10:22.860
The second night and
already it's rainy.

10:22.860 --> 10:23.430
Yeah.

10:23.770 --> 10:25.610
You'll run into some bad weather

10:25.610 --> 10:27.150
if you call on her one
hundred nights in a row.

10:27.150 --> 10:28.420
Good luck.

10:28.420 --> 10:30.690
I'm pretty sure that you
need it more than I do.

10:31.300 --> 10:32.770
Let me know if you can't continue.

10:32.770 --> 10:33.990
I can go by horse instead.

10:33.990 --> 10:37.220
Yes, I'll let you know when
the conditions are bad.

10:38.590 --> 10:40.660
Did you get wet, dear brother?

10:40.660 --> 10:41.780
Please use this.

10:41.780 --> 10:44.890
No.  I'm fine, but my
companion is rather damp.

10:44.890 --> 10:47.260
Oh, dear.  We can't have
you catching cold.

10:47.260 --> 10:48.750
Come with me.

10:49.430 --> 10:51.980
You're more receptive
than I was expecting.

10:51.980 --> 10:54.270
You came all the way through the rain.

10:54.270 --> 10:55.390
It's the right thing to do.

10:56.010 --> 10:57.460
Is this how you received the other men?

10:58.430 --> 11:02.480
No, I never spoke a single word to them.

11:02.850 --> 11:04.540
Really?  That's good.

11:04.540 --> 11:05.180
Huh?

11:05.630 --> 11:07.650
If I'm receiving special treatment,

11:07.650 --> 11:09.650
I probably have a chance, right?

11:09.650 --> 11:11.700
I-It's not like that!

11:11.700 --> 11:12.520
No?

11:13.060 --> 11:16.600
Since you're seeking my hand now,

11:16.600 --> 11:19.020
I have something to tell you.

11:19.790 --> 11:20.680
What's that?

11:21.140 --> 11:23.280
Well, in the event...

11:23.280 --> 11:24.890
In the event that we do get married,

11:25.430 --> 11:28.160
I want you to let me work in the palace.

11:29.310 --> 11:32.170
It's my dream to show important
officials around the palace.

11:33.140 --> 11:35.780
I want to be present and learn

11:35.780 --> 11:39.090
as they speak of poetry and beauty.

11:40.090 --> 11:43.750
Well?  It will help me become a
wife who will make you proud.

11:44.350 --> 11:46.190
I wouldn't recommend it.

11:47.660 --> 11:51.150
The men in the palace are
bound to notice you.

11:51.440 --> 11:54.190
I don't want you attracting
the Emperor's attention.

11:54.880 --> 11:58.310
If you enjoy poetry, we can
compile our own anthology.

11:58.310 --> 11:59.940
I'm willing to help.

12:00.580 --> 12:05.100
I want you to be a wife who
quietly waits for my return.

12:05.560 --> 12:10.230
But I don't want to stay in
this small, little world.

12:10.230 --> 12:12.990
I want to talk to other people
and improve my writing.

12:14.090 --> 12:16.840
You have a high opinion of
the palace, little girl.

12:17.380 --> 12:20.840
There's a lot more going on in
the palace than writing poetry.

12:21.540 --> 12:23.220
I understand that.

12:23.220 --> 12:24.680
No, you don't understand.

12:25.270 --> 12:27.860
Here, since the weather is still warm,

12:27.860 --> 12:30.540
I can tell you a scary story
about the palace to cool us down.

12:30.540 --> 12:32.980
If you want to cool off,
you can go stand in the rain!

12:32.980 --> 12:34.310
I'm going to bed!

12:34.560 --> 12:36.140
You don't want to hear my
story about the palace?

12:36.140 --> 12:38.290
I don't want to hear it!  Good night!

12:41.470 --> 12:44.450
She still has the mindset of a child.

12:47.700 --> 12:52.050
So spring ends and summer comes,

12:52.050 --> 12:55.210
now white robes hang to
dry on Mount Amanokagu.

12:56.060 --> 12:57.830
That's a poem by Empress Jito.

12:57.830 --> 13:02.930
Yes, I really like the
poem and the poet.

13:03.860 --> 13:06.490
A woman became the
ruler of this country.

13:06.900 --> 13:08.390
I think that's wonderful.

13:08.390 --> 13:10.330
Do you want to become Empress, Yoshiko?

13:10.330 --> 13:13.620
Yes, that would make me the
most important person.

13:13.620 --> 13:15.850
Don't you ever think of such things?

13:17.300 --> 13:22.080
Mother said that you're the
grandson of Emperor Kammu.

13:22.630 --> 13:25.270
Doesn't that mean you
can become Emperor?

13:25.270 --> 13:29.080
I can't.  My father
wasn't even a prince.

13:29.520 --> 13:31.680
Wasn't he the son of the Emperor?

13:32.790 --> 13:34.730
You'll understand when you grow up.

13:35.240 --> 13:37.430
A woman will never get
to rule this country,

13:37.430 --> 13:39.180
and neither will I.

13:39.180 --> 13:42.380
Oh, that's no fun...

13:42.740 --> 13:46.610
What does a woman have to
do to become important?

13:48.750 --> 13:50.850
She can't become Empress,

13:50.850 --> 13:53.980
so she wants to make a name
for herself in the palace?

13:55.170 --> 13:57.270
Ninety-eight more nights...

13:58.130 --> 13:59.990
I'll have to convince
her to change her mind.

14:08.150 --> 14:10.530
It's gotten much cooler.

14:10.730 --> 14:14.260
Yes, is it becoming too
difficult to make this trip?

14:14.260 --> 14:15.500
Not at all.

14:15.500 --> 14:17.710
I'm prepared to join you
for a hundred nights,

14:17.710 --> 14:19.840
or a thousand nights,
if that's what it takes.

14:19.840 --> 14:20.880
A thousand nights...

14:22.380 --> 14:23.750
Listen to me, Yoshiko.

14:23.750 --> 14:27.010
Palace life is not as
easy as you think.

14:27.010 --> 14:29.030
I don't expect it to be easy.

14:29.820 --> 14:32.490
My grandmother was allowed
to give birth to my

14:32.490 --> 14:33.960
father at the Emperor's grace.

14:33.960 --> 14:37.170
She was shunned by the Emperor's
wives for being a servant

14:37.170 --> 14:38.830
and suffered greatly.

14:39.300 --> 14:42.090
Your palace rank would
barely be higher than a servant.

14:42.090 --> 14:44.020
You would also suffer,

14:44.780 --> 14:46.670
just like my grandmother did.

14:46.670 --> 14:48.320
You can't scare me.

14:48.320 --> 14:49.960
I'm prepared to suffer.

14:49.960 --> 14:51.440
My mind is made up.

14:54.640 --> 14:56.580
We're well into autumn.

14:56.580 --> 14:58.120
The harvest festival is soon.

14:58.710 --> 15:04.620
Yet she seems to grow more
stubborn every day...

15:07.160 --> 15:09.330
You're in foul humor, again.

15:09.330 --> 15:10.510
Would you like some momiji?

15:11.020 --> 15:13.970
If you agree to let me serve in
the palace, I'll accept them.

15:14.380 --> 15:15.720
Then you don't get any.

15:17.760 --> 15:20.440
Yoshiko, when you were little,

15:20.690 --> 15:23.540
you said you wanted to become
Empress and be important.

15:24.680 --> 15:27.800
I can't believe you still remember that.

15:27.800 --> 15:29.300
I remember everything about you.

15:30.780 --> 15:33.160
Is that why you want
to enter the palace?

15:33.450 --> 15:34.940
You want to be important?

15:34.940 --> 15:36.160
Yes,

15:36.750 --> 15:39.000
I suppose I want to
become more important,

15:39.000 --> 15:40.300
but it's not that simple.

15:40.820 --> 15:42.330
I thought about marriage as well,

15:43.120 --> 15:46.420
and being loved by a man like you.

15:46.650 --> 15:48.440
Though I'm sure you would be unfaithful.

15:48.440 --> 15:49.890
Uh, how can you be so sure?

15:49.890 --> 15:51.760
You'll probably be unfaithful,

15:52.460 --> 15:56.640
but if I could retain my pride,
maintain the house,

15:56.640 --> 16:00.110
raise the children, be myself,
and make my name known,

16:00.110 --> 16:02.780
that would be very wonderful.

16:03.400 --> 16:07.230
However, I would be ignoring
much of my potential.

16:07.920 --> 16:11.470
Would I have an opportunity
to use everything I've learned?

16:11.470 --> 16:14.240
All the knowledge I've obtained?

16:14.720 --> 16:17.660
Or would it all go to waste?

16:18.700 --> 16:21.070
I wouldn't be able to live with that.

16:22.080 --> 16:26.630
I want to do as much as I can
with the life I've been given,

16:26.630 --> 16:29.710
even if it means I must suffer!

16:30.720 --> 16:34.680
If you were a man,
I would support your dream,

16:35.190 --> 16:36.510
but you're a woman,

16:36.900 --> 16:38.490
and a very beautiful one.

16:39.420 --> 16:41.340
You think of women as

16:41.340 --> 16:44.730
pitiful creatures who
need to be protected.

16:45.050 --> 16:46.690
I can't deny that.

16:46.690 --> 16:50.110
That's how women are
treated in this age.

16:50.610 --> 16:53.280
You're mature enough to realize that.

16:54.210 --> 16:57.060
Why must you choose
a path of suffering?

16:57.540 --> 16:59.860
Don't you want to be happy?

16:59.860 --> 17:01.300
I do,

17:01.300 --> 17:03.920
but I'm not looking for someone
else to make me happy!

17:03.920 --> 17:06.670
I want to find my own happiness!

17:07.230 --> 17:08.520
I don't want to become a woman

17:08.520 --> 17:11.400
who only waits, who
needs to be protected!

17:11.820 --> 17:14.700
It made me sad every time you say

17:14.700 --> 17:15.800
that is what you want!

17:16.250 --> 17:18.330
Why don't you understand?!

17:21.080 --> 17:23.680
I left after our fight last night.

17:23.680 --> 17:25.980
I didn't realize she was so stubborn.

17:26.920 --> 17:28.930
Well, I suppose she was always stubborn.

17:28.930 --> 17:31.850
Munesada-dono, the lady
has summoned you!

17:31.850 --> 17:33.570
Yes, I'll be right there.

17:34.920 --> 17:36.910
If she's really so determined,

17:36.910 --> 17:38.820
she'll be able to survive in the palace.

17:43.750 --> 17:45.690
No, that would be...

17:46.370 --> 17:49.060
If I have to let her go before
our future even begins,

17:49.060 --> 17:51.080
I would prefer that she was
wedded to the Emperor.

17:56.950 --> 17:58.430
Of course...

17:58.430 --> 18:00.760
The perfect night for it to storm.

18:01.480 --> 18:03.480
This would be the hundredth night,

18:04.900 --> 18:08.000
but I doubt we'll reach
any sort of agreement.

18:10.320 --> 18:12.150
It's finally the hundredth night?

18:12.460 --> 18:14.810
You were able to hang in there.

18:14.810 --> 18:17.190
Sorry about putting you
through all this trouble.

18:17.190 --> 18:18.390
Don't worry about me.

18:18.390 --> 18:21.680
I would be happy to see
my master find true love.

18:24.030 --> 18:25.910
I can only hope that I am so fortunate.

18:31.280 --> 18:32.510
Munesada-sama!

18:35.910 --> 18:37.630
My dear brother's dead?!

18:37.630 --> 18:40.140
The bridge was swept away
by the rising river,

18:40.140 --> 18:41.640
and he was most likely carried away.

18:42.090 --> 18:44.230
They were able to find the carriage...

18:46.650 --> 18:47.980
Yoshiko-sama!

18:47.980 --> 18:49.190
Where are you going?

18:49.190 --> 18:50.820
I'm going to look for him!

18:50.820 --> 18:51.550
You mustn't!

18:51.550 --> 18:52.610
Release me!

19:02.420 --> 19:04.160
You finally let me see your face.

19:04.610 --> 19:05.750
Dear brother?

19:06.290 --> 19:07.810
Is it really you?

19:08.740 --> 19:10.780
You thought I wouldn't
come because of the rain?

19:10.780 --> 19:12.920
The bridge was swept away
and your carriage...

19:13.270 --> 19:15.680
I was thrown out before the
carriage was carried away.

19:15.680 --> 19:16.990
As you can see, I'm fine.

19:18.530 --> 19:19.570
Excuse me.

19:19.570 --> 19:21.480
My servant is shivering outside,

19:21.480 --> 19:22.800
so could you please look after him?

19:22.800 --> 19:24.130
Yes, at once.

19:24.130 --> 19:26.200
That's right.  Wait, dear brother.

19:26.200 --> 19:27.470
I'll bring some hot water.

19:27.470 --> 19:28.100
Hold on.

19:29.310 --> 19:30.590
You're coming with me.

19:30.590 --> 19:31.480
Huh?

19:32.790 --> 19:34.800
There, that's one hundred nights.

19:35.370 --> 19:37.440
Too bad for you, Yoshiko.

19:37.440 --> 19:38.770
I'm so glad!

19:38.770 --> 19:40.420
I'm sorry!  I'm sorry!

19:40.420 --> 19:45.050
You almost died because
I was being silly!

19:45.050 --> 19:46.580
It's okay.  I'm fine.

19:47.250 --> 19:49.550
Stop crying.  Let me see your face.

19:51.890 --> 19:54.790
I finally get to see your
face, but it's so ugly.

19:54.790 --> 19:56.090
That's mean!

19:56.090 --> 19:56.750
Just kidding.

19:57.500 --> 19:59.420
You're even beautiful when you're crying.

20:05.190 --> 20:06.310
I'm sorry...

20:09.980 --> 20:11.000
Come here.

20:14.130 --> 20:15.690
Must it be so?

20:16.240 --> 20:18.110
One hundred nights weren't enough

20:18.110 --> 20:19.280
to prove my love?

20:20.180 --> 20:21.470
Do you dislike me?

20:22.480 --> 20:23.360
I love you.

20:23.820 --> 20:25.190
I love you so much.

20:25.190 --> 20:27.050
I've loved you since I was a child.

20:27.050 --> 20:28.290
Why won't you accept me?

20:29.730 --> 20:32.680
I spent the past one
hundred nights thinking.

20:33.230 --> 20:35.300
If I had a future in which you loved me

20:35.300 --> 20:38.880
and we could build a life together,
I wished to see it become reality.

20:39.360 --> 20:45.260
but I couldn't bring myself
to give up on my dream.

20:46.630 --> 20:49.750
I've put you through so much trouble
to come here all these nights.

20:49.750 --> 20:51.060
I'm sorry.

20:51.770 --> 20:55.570
Could you pretend that
you didn't come tonight?

20:56.130 --> 20:56.720
No.

20:56.720 --> 20:57.190
Ow!

20:57.940 --> 20:59.630
You promised to become my wife

20:59.630 --> 21:02.150
if I called on you for one hundred nights.

21:15.110 --> 21:16.170
Dear brother...

21:17.760 --> 21:18.960
Fine...

21:19.510 --> 21:22.530
I've lost, Yoshiko.

21:26.300 --> 21:28.930
Ninety-nine nights?

21:28.930 --> 21:32.370
Why couldn't you hang in
there one more night?!

21:32.370 --> 21:33.860
I wagered money on you!

21:33.860 --> 21:37.070
It was storming so hard
that I would have died.

21:37.070 --> 21:37.860
Damn...

21:38.480 --> 21:42.030
However, you were right, Munesada-dono.

21:42.030 --> 21:45.920
Yoshizane-dono's daughter is beautiful.

21:47.600 --> 21:50.830
This may be the last
time I ever see her.

21:51.950 --> 21:56.120
The sky is the road home
for the holy maidens,

21:56.590 --> 21:59.770
may the wind bring clouds
to extend their stay.

22:01.480 --> 22:07.590
Oh wind, please blow strongly and
seal the holy maiden's road home.

22:08.660 --> 22:12.460
I wish to look at her a while longer.

22:14.820 --> 22:17.540
I do not know where your
dream will take you,

22:18.390 --> 22:21.550
but I pray for your happiness.

22:23.910 --> 22:26.330
Yoshiko entered the palace as
one of the Emperor's brides.

22:27.530 --> 22:31.120
She would later become
known as Ono no Komachi.

22:32.910 --> 22:34.910
Poetic Tale 3:

22:32.910 --> 22:34.910
END

24:04.960 --> 24:22.000
Next Episode

24:04.960 --> 24:22.000
Yasuhide and Narihira

24:04.960 --> 24:22.000
Funya no Yasuhide

24:06.730 --> 24:11.390
Gust of wind leaves fall leaves falling,

24:12.160 --> 24:15.950
hence the name fall leaves.
